(begin-tx "DPOF-G3a — DPOF|C>DEBIT: the list-arity gate that fronts every wipe and transmit")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPOF-G3a · 01 · debit arity] ---")
;;These are defcaps, so the obvious route in is a full Talos transfer. `test-capability` acquires
;;a capability directly and runs its body, and these enforces sit above every read — so dummy ids
;;reach them and the guards cost nothing.
;;
;;Each case takes its own transaction: a granted capability is cached for the rest of the tx, so
;;re-acquiring the same one returns the grant WITHOUT re-running the body.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<DPOF-G3a>> one nonce against two amounts is refused before anything is read"
            "Invalid Inputs for Debitation"
            (test-capability (DPOF.DPOF|C>DEBIT "a" "b" [1] [1.0 2.0] false)))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "DPOF-G3b — DPOF|C>CREDIT: a nonce chain that is neither singular nor consecutive")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPOF-G3b · 01 · credit nonce chain] ---")
;;Crediting admits exactly two shapes: a SINGULAR chain (one nonce that already exists) or a
;;CONSECUTIVE one (a run starting immediately after the last used nonce). [1 5 9] on a live
;;ortofungible is neither, so the enforce-one exhausts both branches and reports its own message.
;;
;;A real id is required here — unlike DPOF-G3a, both predicates READ (UR_IzNonce / UR_NoncesUsed),
;;so a dummy id would abort in the read rather than reach the guard.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<DPOF-G3b>> a gapped nonce chain matches neither admitted shape"
            "Invalid Nonce Chain for Creditation"
            (test-capability (DPOF.DPOF|C>CREDIT "a" "MOCKO-98c486052a51"
                [1 5 9] [1.0 1.0 1.0] [[{"a":1}] [{"a":1}] [{"a":1}]])))
    ]
)
;;FINDING — the two enforces INSIDE those branches are unreachable, and this is a proof rather
;;than an observation:
;;
;;    (if iz-singular    (do (enforce (not iz-consecutive) "…must compute false for Consecutive") …))
;;    (if iz-consecutive (do (enforce (not iz-singular)    "…must compute false for Singular")    …))
;;
;;Each fires only if BOTH predicates are true at once. They cannot be:
;;
;;    UC_IzSingular    = (length = 1) AND the nonce EXISTS
;;    UC_IzConsecutive = the run starts at nonces-used + 1, i.e. the nonces DO NOT exist yet
;;
;;For length 1, consecutive means the nonce is exactly nonces-used + 1 — by definition not yet
;;used — so UR_IzNonce is false and singular is false. For length > 1 singular is false anyway.
;;The two are mutually exclusive for every input, so both enforces are fail-closed backstops.
;;Confirmed against this suite's live state (nonces-used = 1, nonce 1 exists): [1] is singular and
;;not consecutive, [2] is consecutive and not singular. Annotated at the source.
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "DPOF-G3c — DPOF|C>UPDATE-SPECIAL: the vesting/sleeping/hibernation tag")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPOF-G3c · 01 · vzh tag domain] ---")
;;The tag selects WHICH special linkage is being updated — 1 vesting, 2 sleeping, 3 hibernation —
;;and it is the first line of the cap, above every read. An out-of-domain tag would otherwise fall
;;through the cond to BAR and update the wrong linkage, so the guard is doing real work here even
;;though every in-tree caller passes a literal.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<DPOF-G3c>> a tag outside 1..3 is refused"
            "Invalid Vesting|Sleeping|Hibernation Tag"
            (test-capability (DPOF.DPOF|C>UPDATE-SPECIAL "a" "b" 9)))
        (expect-failure "<<DPOF-G3c>> ...and so is zero, one below the domain"
            "Invalid Vesting|Sleeping|Hibernation Tag"
            (test-capability (DPOF.DPOF|C>UPDATE-SPECIAL "a" "b" 0)))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

